From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:32:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: page translation drawn by the shell

Plan B47. Chrome's translate component (ChromeTranslateClient,
TranslateManager, TranslateAgent with Google's Translate Element) runs
on every bridge tab unchanged; only its Views bubble is replaced.

- TranslateBubbleFactory::SetFactory() (Chrome's hook, used whenever no
  Browser holds the tab) routes every translate step to a per-tab
  openarc::TranslateTabHelper, which folds the steps and Chrome's
  LanguageState into one state (available, translating, translated,
  failed, with source and target language) for the shell.
- Commands run as Chrome's bubble does (TranslateUIDelegate): translate
  into the offered or a chosen language, revert, never translate this
  site; OACProfile resets the profile's TranslatePrefs.
- TranslateManager offers translation only with Google API keys. The
  Translate Element library Google serves to websites carries its own
  key, so the gate is lifted (SetIgnoreMissingKeyForTesting); verified
  against translate.googleapis.com without keys of our own.
- TFLite language detection is disabled in every process (the model is
  never downloaded here); CLD3 detects pages without a lang attribute.
- Public API: OACTranslation.h (OACTranslationState,
  OACTranslationLanguage, OACTab / OACProfile / OACApplication
  categories) and -[OACTabDelegate tabDidChangeTranslationState:].
---
